Bluetooth: request only Role Switch and Sniff in the default link policy

The Unisoc Marlin3 (SC2355) firmware advertises LMP Hold Mode and Park
State in its feature mask, but answers HCI_Write_Default_Link_Policy_Settings
with "Invalid HCI Command Parameters" (0x12) whenever HCI_LP_HOLD or
HCI_LP_PARK is set (0x0000, 0x0001, 0x0004 and 0x0005 are accepted, 0x0007
is rejected). The failure aborts the controller init and makes
"hciconfig hci0 up" / bluetoothd power-on fail with -EINVAL.

Park State was removed from the Core specification in 5.0 and Hold Mode is
not used by BlueZ, so never request either.

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
index 21469934f..2f5b14861 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
@@ -504,12 +504,8 @@ static void hci_setup_link_policy(struct hci_request *req)
 
 	if (lmp_rswitch_capable(hdev))
 		link_policy |= HCI_LP_RSWITCH;
-	if (lmp_hold_capable(hdev))
-		link_policy |= HCI_LP_HOLD;
 	if (lmp_sniff_capable(hdev))
 		link_policy |= HCI_LP_SNIFF;
-	if (lmp_park_capable(hdev))
-		link_policy |= HCI_LP_PARK;
 
 	cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy);
 	hci_req_add(req, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY, sizeof(cp), &cp);
